# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and checked out as LF
# everywhere.
#
# Without this, the two platforms disagree: a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true produces CRLF working-tree files, while the WSL checkout of
# the same commit stays LF. Editing from Windows and diffing from WSL then shows
# every line as changed -- a 568-line change once measured as 2221 insertions.
#
# `eol=lf` (rather than plain `text=auto`) is deliberate: it pins the working
# tree to LF on all platforms, so both sides see the same bytes and the
# autocrlf setting stops mattering. Every tracked file here is text, so `auto`
# never has to guess.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Lockfiles and version pins stay LF and are never rewritten by editors.
uv.lock text eol=lf
.python-version text eol=lf
